lang: sql
name: SQL
ext: sql
mode: browser
runtime: SQLite 3 compiled to WebAssembly (sql.js); a fresh database for every run
run: sqlite3 soc.db < kata.sql
blurb: Threat hunting in SQL. Every kata runs against the same small SOC database: users, login events, hosts and alerts. Your result set is compared with the reference query's.
notes: Tables: users(id, name, dept, is_admin), logins(id, user_id, ts, ip, success), hosts(id, hostname, os), alerts(id, host_id, ts, severity, rule). ts is ISO-8601 text, success and is_admin are 0/1, severity is 1-5. Column names in your output don't have to match, but column count and values do.

schema:
  CREATE TABLE users(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT, dept TEXT, is_admin INTEGER);
  CREATE TABLE logins(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, user_id INTEGER, ts TEXT, ip TEXT, success INTEGER);
  CREATE TABLE hosts(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, hostname TEXT, os TEXT);
  CREATE TABLE alerts(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, host_id INTEGER, ts TEXT, severity INTEGER, rule TEXT);
